def texescape(s):
 table={'\\':r'\textbackslash{}','&':r'\&','%':r'\%','$':r'\$','#':r'\#','_':r'\_','{':r'\{','}':r'\}','~':r'\textasciitilde{}','^':r'\textasciicircum{}','–':'--','—':'---','×':r'$\times$','−':'-','≥':r'$\geq$','≤':r'$\leq$','’':"'",'“':'``','”':"''"};out=''.join(table.get(c,c) for c in str(s))
 import re
 for token in re.findall(r'(?:tables/)?[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_./-]*\.(?:jsonl|json|md|tex|pdf)',str(s)):
  escaped=''.join(table.get(c,c) for c in token);out=out.replace(escaped,r'\path{'+token+'}')
 return out
def figure(name,caption,width='.96'):
 return {'kind':'figure','name':name,'caption':clean_prose(caption),'width':width}
def clean_prose(text):
 import re
 text=re.sub(r'\b(The|the|All|all|not|and|with|has|versus|from|to|under|absolute|relative|linear|step|steps|seed|seeds|block|Block|candidate|Candidate|through)(?=\d)',r'\1 ',text)
 text=re.sub(r'\b(Conditional|conditional|paired)(?=95%)',r'\1 ',text)
 text=re.sub(r'(?<=\d)(?=(?:candidates|candidate|tasks|task|representations|records|intervals|CV|units|rows|points|paths|figures|seeds|groups|validation|source))',' ',text)
 text=re.sub(r':(?=\d)',': ',text)
 text=text.replace('task/split/metric/readout/policy/seed','task, split, metric, readout, policy and seed dimensions')
 return text
blocks=[]
def section(title,*paragraphs):blocks.append({'kind':'section','title':title});blocks.extend({'kind':'paragraph','text':clean_prose(p)} for p in paragraphs)
title='Layerwise benign evaluation across nine supplied saliency-sweep checkpoints'
subtitle='Verified retain results with recovered, scientifically unqualified forget-related source logs'
abstract=(f'We report {cov["classifier_metric_records"]:,} released classifier metric records across nine supplied checkpoints, six benign tasks, all 26 representations, three probe CV partitions and two distinct readout policies. Refitted probes and unchanged original-base probes answer different questions. At both emphasized representations, refitted AUROC exceeds the unchanged readout in {g["positive"]} of {g["n"]} candidate/task/anchor/seed comparisons, with point gaps {val(g["min"])} to {val(g["max"])}; {g["CI_includes_zero"]} existing pointwise intervals include zero. Refitted block16 AUROC exceeds final normalization descriptively in {a["above"]} of {a["n"]} candidate/task/seed combinations. Relative to the original pretrained base, results remain task-, layer-, metric- and policy-dependent, including adverse and inconclusive findings. Recovered forget logs contain 23 step-axis validation-loss observations, but no currently qualified scientific aggregate, checkpoint-matched comparison or layerwise forget-performance result. This report completes a bounded reporting scope; the original retain-and-forget request remains partial.')
section('Abstract',abstract)
section('Questions and evidence scope','The scientific questions are whether the six benign labels remain accessible to the chosen linear classifiers, whether the original scaler/readout remains compatible with each supplied endpoint, how those answers vary over representations, and how sequence prediction differs descriptively from classification. The separate forget question requires source qualification that is not established by benign scores or source-log integrity.','The reporting plan fixes question-based organization, deterministic candidate/task/layer order, block16 and final-normalization emphasis, seed42 as a display convention, and the H3 primary plus multiclass-splice examples. All seeds remain in the complete tables and atlas. Prior outcomes were visible; this reporting plan is not a scientific preregistration. No new experiment, fit, model forward, resampling draw, threshold, calibration or inferential comparison is introduced.')
blocks.append(figure('STUDY_SCOPE','Completed retain-evaluation design and the separate status of source-log forget evidence. CV partitions are not independent intervention replications.'))
section('Checkpoint and task identities','Registry aliases candidate_01 through candidate_09 identify exact delivered tensor content, not old R labels or known intervention parents. Both noise5 endpoints remain distinct at steps2000 and2151. Folder labels and nominal percentages describe the supplied naming scheme; they do not prove perturbation masks, realized dose, objective or training exposure. Candidate identities, checkpoint steps and source hashes are retained in every classification table and in REPORTING_FACTS.json.','Tasks are emp_H3, gue_tf_0, gue_prom_core_all, gue_prom_300_all, gue_splice_reconstructed and gue_mouse_0. Human-readable labels in figures are conservative renderings of these identifiers, not inferred biological aliases. The primary classification split is DEV: H3 has1497 rows/1497 exact-or-reverse-complement groups; the other tasks have512 rows, with511 such groups for reconstructed splice. Numeric classes are0/1 for binary tasks and0/1/2 for splice. No untouched test data were opened.','Representations are decoder.layers.0 through decoder.layers.24 and decoder.final_norm, each width1920 in the qualified extractor. The zero-based decoder.layers.16 is the seventeenth decoder block. Final normalization is a separate representation. All26 remain available; emphasis is not a global optimum claim.')
blocks.append({'kind':'candidate_table'})
section('Central analysis pipeline and readout policies','Previously completed S05–S08 extraction used the qualified frozen native Evo2-1B backend, masked mean nucleotide pooling and preserved tokenizer/preprocessing/loading identities. S09 independently released the saved-output contrasts. S11 derives reporting records from those releases and verification overlays, not from an unverified producer status string. Original producer receipts remain historical; the explicit release overlay controls reuse.','Independent refit uses each endpoint\'s TRAIN features and the frozen balanced L2 logistic-regression procedure. C is selected from0.1/1/10 using mean fold AUROC, with exact ties going to smaller C. H3 uses three folds; other tasks use five; CV seeds42/17/1234 identify the recovered fixed StratifiedGroupKFold partitions. Scaling is fold-local during selection and refitted on all TRAIN rows for the final classifier. The established LBFGS tolerance/retry procedure is unchanged. H3 TRAIN has11971 rows; other TRAIN cohorts have1024 each.','Fixed original base applies the exact saved pretrained-base StandardScaler and classifier unchanged to each candidate. It does not recenter, recalibrate, fit a parent head or refit on target features. Refitted performance measures label accessibility under this classifier family and fitting protocol. Fixed-base performance measures compatibility with that original scaler/readout. Neither measures complete task information or proves erasure.','The five classifier metrics are AUROC, AP, accuracy, balanced accuracy and classifier cross-entropy. Binary positive class is numeric1 with fixed threshold0.5; multiclass splice uses sorted class order, macro one-vs-rest AUROC, mean classwise AP, argmax accuracy and macro recall. Cross-entropy uses inherited float64-epsilon clipping. AUROC/AP are ranking measures; threshold decisions and probability loss can disagree. Classifier cross-entropy is nats per labeled example. Actual-head LM NLL is nats per valid next-token target and must remain separate.')
section('Statistical interpretation','All admitted comparisons reuse the original2000 exact/RC-group draws, bootstrap seed20261103, original row/group/class order and explicit common valid-draw masks. Candidate-minus-reference effects are computed within the same draws. Intervals are the original linear2.5th/97.5th percentiles:95% pointwise exploratory intervals conditional on the fitted readouts and cohorts. They omit intervention-training variability and fitting uncertainty and do not provide a familywise guarantee across this grid.','An interval crossing zero is inconclusive; it is not equivalence or proof of no change. A positive point is not automatically a confidently positive effect. Seed ranges are descriptive partition sensitivity, not confidence intervals or independent intervention replication. Paired-effect intervals are not obtained by subtracting marginal endpoints. Exact/RC grouping does not establish locus, homology or biological independence.','The released inferential inventory is42,120 original-base comparisons,6,480 anchor DNA-control comparisons and324 anchor policy gaps. The42,228 deferred specifications remain inactive:42,120 immediate-parent comparisons and108 exact LM-base comparisons. Original-base references are qualified comparison baselines, not established immediate parents. Composition and normalized forward4-mer references are simple DNA controls, reused with exact saved heads and cohort/draw associations; outperforming them is not biological understanding.')
section('Results: refitting and original-readout compatibility',f'At the two fixed anchors, refitted AUROC minus unchanged-base AUROC is positive in {g["positive"]} of all {g["n"]} records. The composition is9 candidates ×6 tasks ×2 anchors ×3 CV seeds. Gaps range from {val(g["min"])} to {val(g["max"])}; {g["CI_includes_zero"]} paired pointwise intervals include zero. These dependent records support a consistent difference between readout policies at the observed anchors, not a causal account of how the intervention changed representations. Evidence: claim policy_gap.','A label can remain accessible after the prescribed refitting procedure even when the original head transfers poorly. This distinction is especially visible on some promoter and TF endpoints. It does not prove all task information is preserved, explain an intervention mechanism or demonstrate relearning. The full all-layer atlas keeps all candidates and all CV partitions rather than selecting the largest gap.')
blocks.append(figure('ANCHOR_READOUT_GAPS','Every candidate, task, anchor and CV seed is shown. Error bars are the already released paired95% pointwise conditional intervals. Readout gap is not a universally desirable scientific score.'))
section('Results: representations and all-layer context',f'For refitted DEV AUROC, block16 exceeds final normalization in {a["above"]} of {a["n"]} candidate/task/CV-seed combinations:9 ×6 ×3. This is a descriptive comparison of released point values; no new layer-to-layer test or interval is constructed. It does not establish block16 as the globally best layer. Evidence: claim anchor_layer.','The complete atlas retains25 decoder-block outputs and final normalization, every classifier metric, both policies and all three CV seeds. Layer shapes and reference-relative effects can vary by task and policy. The atlas uses small multiples and source-linked full-resolution exports; the main report uses the predeclared anchors for readability rather than hiding the intervening layers.')
blocks.append({'kind':'anchor_range_table'})
section('Results: original-base effects include adverse findings','The reference question differs from the readout-policy question. A refitted candidate can outperform its own unchanged-base readout while still performing below the pretrained-base endpoint. The fixed H3 and multiclass-splice examples use candidate01, block16 and CV seed42; candidate01 is the first registry alias, not a winner selected by performance.',f'H3 refitted AUROC has candidate-minus-base difference {effect("example_emp_H3_independent_refit")}; H3 unchanged-base AUROC has difference {effect("example_emp_H3_fixed_original_base")}. For splice, the corresponding differences are {effect("example_gue_splice_reconstructed_independent_refit")} and {effect("example_gue_splice_reconstructed_fixed_original_base")}. Brackets show existing paired95% pointwise conditional intervals. These are exact endpoint/reference comparisons, not immediate-parent or selective-unlearning effects. Evidence: the four example claims.','Across the full grid there are favorable, adverse, exactly equal and interval-inconclusive comparisons. Summaries in tables/BASE_COMPARISON_SUMMARY.jsonl preserve task, policy, metric, denominator and exact source IDs. Such row counts are coverage summaries, not percentages of capabilities retained. The6480 frozen DNA-control contrasts remain reference-specific and anchor-limited; they are not extrapolated into full-layer control inference.')
blocks.append(figure('ORIGINAL_BASE_EFFECTS','All9 candidate endpoints in fixed H3/splice examples, both readout policies, block16 and seed42. Sign is candidate minus original pretrained base. Every adverse and inconclusive interval remains visible.'))
section('Results: ranking, probability quality and seed sensitivity',f'At {dis["n"]} of {dis["eligible_prediction_cells"]:,} candidate/task/representation/seed/policy cells, AUROC is above the base point while classifier cross-entropy is worse (higher). This descriptive conjunction shows that ranking and probability quality cannot substitute for each other. It is not a joint-significance test or capability percentage. Exact paired source IDs are in tables/RANKING_LOSS_DISAGREEMENT.jsonl. Evidence: claim ranking_loss.','Different CV partitions can select the same C and therefore the same final all-TRAIN fit. The inherited seed-sensitivity table exposes coincident values and sign exceptions without choosing the favorable partition. Repeated final heads or predictions do not create independent intervention replications. All source seed groups remain in REPORTING_FACTS.json and the S09 all-layer atlas.')
section('Results: sequence prediction is separate','The108 LM units comprise54 primary DEV and54 diagnostic TRAIN units:9 candidates ×6 tasks ×2 splits. They produce216 NLL/perplexity metric records. They are not108 independent held-out evaluations and are not expanded across probe layers or CV seeds. DEV uses its existing conditional group-bootstrap intervals. TRAIN diagnostics have no invented uncertainty.','Perplexity is exp(aggregated NLL) under the qualified actual output head and valid-target mask. The report does not average across tasks or combine LM loss with classifier cross-entropy. Different task cohorts can exhibit different sequence-prediction losses alongside different classification profiles; this is descriptive coexistence, not a new correlation, causal association or combined capability score. LM original-base comparisons remain deferred, so the figure does not claim an improvement relative to base or parent.')
blocks.append(figure('LM_DEV_RESULTS','All54 primary DEV LM NLL units with existing intervals. Candidate aliases remain categorical; no connected dose trajectory or independent-seed interpretation is introduced. All panels use the same y-axis scale.'))
blocks.append({'kind':'LM_range_table'})
section('Corrected forget-evidence assessment','Forget-related source logs were supplied and recovered. Corrective S10 verified nine event files,418,914,867 source bytes,4,069,391 complete events and4,069,382 scalar observations. There are14,090 step-axis training forget-loss observations,23 step-axis forget-validation-loss observations and23 corresponding step-axis logged validation-ppl values. The92 loss/ppl/both-axis records are not92 independent validation evaluations. Alternate sample-axis series repeat the same observations; nine files are not nine independent training runs.','Reinit5 A contains two distinct forget loss validation values at step1500:1.3953843116760254 and1.3952388763427734. Both remain present; neither is averaged away or selected as the last call. Reinit5 B records training only through1439 with a different validation history. Noise5 step2000 and2151 are distinct delivered endpoints with unresolved exact log-to-content binding, not independent seeds. Configurations declare702 versus1 evaluation iterations, but this does not establish the actual unique-example/valid-target denominator, distributed reduction, masking or exposure.','Transport and scalar extraction are verified, but exact checkpoint/invocation, metric definition/direction, cohort/split, denominator/aggregation and producing implementation identities remain unqualified. Thus there are zero currently qualified scientific forget aggregates, zero checkpoint-matched comparisons and zero qualified layerwise forget-performance observations. Layer-indexed gradient norms are optimization diagnostics. A model-level loss cannot be copied across26 layers to satisfy a layerwise request. Evidence: claim source_forget and the unchanged corrected S10 ledger.','The9 ×26 representation slots are only a coverage illustration. A full forget task/split/metric/readout/policy/seed grid is unspecified; no project completion percentage or fabricated missing-cell denominator is supplied. No retain/forget frontier, successful forgetting, causal selectivity or optimal checkpoint is inferred from source logs. Original scalar names are not relabeled as verified biological metrics or held-out NLL.')
blocks.append(figure('FORGET_SOURCE_REINIT5_A','Source-log evidence; scientifically unqualified. Reinit5 A unsmoothed training and all4 validation observations, including both step1500 values. The complete gallery includes readable individual panels for all9 logs and the unchanged full S10 overview.'))
section('Limitations tied to claims','Unknown immediate parents block intervention-parent effects; comparisons with the qualified original pretrained base remain valid at their actual descriptive reference scope. Unverified saliency masks, perturbation laws and realized doses block mechanistic or calibrated-strength comparisons; the supplied endpoint measurements remain valid. Endpoint-step/exposure differences block controlled dose-response or method attribution; both noise5 identities remain separate.','Independent intervention replication is not established. Probe CV seeds and source files cannot fill that gap; conditional readout/cohort descriptions remain valid. Unqualified forget semantics and content binding block scientific retain/forget integration; source integrity, original-tag quotations and duplicate diagnostics remain usable. Missing layerwise forget performance blocks the original layerwise combined conclusion; it does not invalidate the verified layerwise benign measurements.','Whole-delivery inventory remains PARTIAL, so nine selected endpoints are not an exhaustive sweep claim. Candidate05 historical upload privacy remains unknown; current private protection is verified separately and cannot retroactively establish original visibility. Recovery verifies exact archived bytes and the declared sampled saved-analysis panel, not all model execution, biological truth, fresh GPU replay or a clean scientific-runtime rebuild. R2 was not produced and is excluded. Pod B relearning remains separate. No-deadline continuity is preserved.')
section('Reproducibility and future evidence intake','REPORTING_FACTS.json is the common numerical source for this report, the reviewer briefing, tables and new figures. CLAIM_LEDGER.jsonl binds every headline and fixed numerical example to exact source IDs, scope, metric direction, intervals or explicit lack of uncertainty, and interpretation limits. TABLE_INDEX.json gives full-precision table paths and hashes; FIGURE_SOURCE_MAP.json binds individual displayed coordinates to source keys; FIGURE_GALLERY.md indexes the complete immutable atlas.','Fresh CPU recovery uses the unchanged original S05 and S08 saved-head selectors:252 paths spanning every candidate/task, both policies, both emphasized representations and all CV seeds across the panel, including multiclass splice. The full seed crossproduct is not crossed within each unit. Saved scalers/heads and selected features reproduce probabilities; original draws reproduce metrics/vectors/intervals. Tolerances remain absolute1e-10 for probabilities and1e-12 for metric/draw/interval values, relative zero. See FRESH_CPU_RESTORE_CHECK.json for actual scope, worst residuals and locations; byte verification, sampled numerical reconstruction, reporting regeneration, unperformed GPU replay and unperformed clean-runtime recreation are explicitly separate.','New checkpoint/log invocation bindings or evaluation/cohort/aggregation metadata require a separately versioned S10 qualification assessment. Compatible reference aggregates affect only eligible reference claims. Genuine layerwise aggregates require their own task/readout/hook/protocol qualification. A corrected source creates a new immutable source version and invalidates only its dependent joins/claims/figures; unaffected retain science remains reusable. The concise collaborator request remains unsent. No future stage or workflow starts automatically.')
section('Conclusion','Under the chosen frozen classifier family, benign label accessibility after refitting and compatibility with the original readout are distinct empirical properties. Their differences vary across tasks and representations and coexist with adverse, flat and inconclusive original-base results. Sequence prediction is a separate task-specific measurement. The recovered forget logs establish supplied source observations, not qualified forgetting or layerwise forget performance. Reporting can finish for this evidence scope while the original retain-and-forget request remains partial.')
def markdown(blocks):
 out=['# '+title,'',subtitle,'']
 for b in blocks:
  if b['kind']=='section':out+=['## '+b['title'],'']
  elif b['kind']=='paragraph':out+=[b['text'],'']
  elif b['kind']=='figure':out+=['!['+b['name']+'](figures/'+b['name']+'.png)','',b['caption'],'']
  elif b['kind']=='candidate_table':
   out+=['| Alias | Supplied label | Step |','|---|---|---:|']+[f'| {r["alias"]} | {r["label"]} | {r["step"]} |' for r in f['candidates']]+['']
  elif b['kind']=='anchor_range_table':
   out+=['| Task | Policy | Block16 AUROC range | Finalnorm AUROC range |','|---|---|---|---|']
   for t in TASKS:
    for p in f['policies']:
     rr=[next(r for r in f['anchor_ranges'] if (r['task'],r['policy'],r['representation'])==(t,p,rep)) for rep in ['decoder.layers.16','decoder.final_norm']];out.append('| '+LABELS[t]+' | '+('Refit' if p=='independent_refit' else 'Fixed base')+' | '+' | '.join(val(r['min'])+'–'+val(r['max']) for r in rr)+' |')
   out+=['','Each range covers9 candidates ×3 CV seeds; these are descriptive ranges, not confidence intervals.','']
  elif b['kind']=='LM_range_table':
   out+=['| Task | DEV NLL range | DEV perplexity range |','|---|---|---|']
   for t in TASKS:
    rr=[next(r for r in f['LM_DEV_ranges'] if (r['task'],r['metric'])==(t,m)) for m in ['LM_NLL','LM_PPL']];out.append('| '+LABELS[t]+' | '+' | '.join(val(r['min'])+'–'+val(r['max']) for r in rr)+' |')
   out+=['','Ranges cover9 supplied endpoints; no matched-parent or checkpoint-pair significance claim.','']
 return '\n'.join(out)
def preamble(titletext):return r'''\documentclass[11pt]{article}
\usepackage[margin=0.8in]{geometry}
\usepackage{graphicx,booktabs,longtable,tabularx,xcolor,hyperref,enumitem}
\definecolor{ink}{HTML}{17344D}\definecolor{accent}{HTML}{0072B2}
\hypersetup{colorlinks=true,linkcolor=ink,urlcolor=accent,pdftitle={'''+texescape(titletext)+r'''},pdfauthor={Pod A saliency study}}
\emergencystretch=2em\setlength{\parindent}{0pt}\setlength{\parskip}{6pt}\setlist{nosep,leftmargin=*}
\renewcommand{\arraystretch}{1.18}
\begin{document}
'''
def latextable(b):
 k=b['kind'];o=[r'\begin{center}\small']
 if k=='candidate_table':
  o+=[r'\begin{tabularx}{\textwidth}{lXr}\toprule Alias & Supplied label (not verified mechanism) & Step\\\midrule']
  for r in f['candidates']:o.append(texescape(r['alias'])+' & '+r'\path{'+r['label']+'}'+' & '+str(r['step'])+r'\\')
 elif k=='anchor_range_table':
  o+=[r'\begin{tabularx}{\textwidth}{Xlrr}\toprule Task & Readout & Block16 range & Finalnorm range\\\midrule']
  for t in TASKS:
   for p in f['policies']:
    rr=[next(r for r in f['anchor_ranges'] if (r['task'],r['policy'],r['representation'])==(t,p,rep)) for rep in ['decoder.layers.16','decoder.final_norm']];o.append(texescape(LABELS[t])+' & '+('Refit' if p=='independent_refit' else 'Fixed')+' & '+' & '.join(val(r['min'])+'--'+val(r['max']) for r in rr)+r'\\')
 else:
  o+=[r'\begin{tabularx}{\textwidth}{Xrr}\toprule Task & DEV NLL range & DEV perplexity range\\\midrule']
  for t in TASKS:
   rr=[next(r for r in f['LM_DEV_ranges'] if (r['task'],r['metric'])==(t,m)) for m in ['LM_NLL','LM_PPL']];o.append(texescape(LABELS[t])+' & '+' & '.join(val(r['min'])+'--'+val(r['max']) for r in rr)+r'\\')
 return '\n'.join(o+[r'\bottomrule\end{tabularx}\end{center}'])
def latex(blocks):
 out=[preamble(title),r'{\Large\bfseries\color{ink} '+texescape(title)+r'}\par',r'{\large '+texescape(subtitle)+r'}\par',r'\textbf{Reporting scope: verified retain evidence; scientific forget integration pending.}\par']
 for b in blocks:
  if b['kind']=='section':out.append(r'\section{'+texescape(b['title'])+'}')
  elif b['kind']=='paragraph':out.append(texescape(b['text'])+r'\par')
  elif b['kind']=='figure':out.append(r'\begin{figure}[p]\centering\includegraphics[width='+b['width']+r'\textwidth,height=.79\textheight,keepaspectratio]{figures/'+b['name']+r'.pdf}\caption{'+texescape(b['caption'])+r'}\end{figure}')
  else:out.append(latextable(b))
 out+=[r'\section*{Complete evidence and source links}',r'\href{TABLE_INDEX.json}{Full-precision tables and source identities}; \href{CLAIM_LEDGER.jsonl}{claim ledger}; \href{FIGURE_GALLERY.md}{complete figure gallery}; \href{FRESH_CPU_RESTORE_CHECK.json}{fresh CPU recovery scope and exact residual locations}; \href{FINAL_RECEIPT.json}{actual delivery identities}.',r'\end{document}'];return '\n'.join(out)+'\n'
(P/'RESULTS.md').write_text(markdown(blocks));(P/'RESULTS.tex').write_text(latex(blocks));save(P/'REPORT_DOCUMENT.json',{'title':title,'subtitle':subtitle,'blocks':blocks,'facts_sha256':sha(P/'REPORTING_FACTS.json'),'claim_ledger_sha256':sha(P/'CLAIM_LEDGER.jsonl')})
review=[{'title':'What we measured, and what can be concluded','paragraphs':[abstract,'The original retain-and-forget request remains PARTIAL. The nine endpoints are supplied checkpoints with unresolved immediate parents, masks, realized dose and exposure. Nothing here establishes successful forgetting.'],'figure':'STUDY_SCOPE'}, {'title':'Two readout questions give different answers','paragraphs':[f'Refitted probes test accessibility under the frozen linear-classifier procedure. Fixed-base probes test compatibility with the exact unchanged original scaler/head. All {g["n"]} anchor AUROC point gaps favor refitting; {g["CI_includes_zero"]} conditional intervals include zero. The324 records are9 candidates ×6 tasks ×2 anchors ×3 CV seeds, not324 independent interventions.',f'Block16 is the seventeenth decoder block. Its refitted AUROC exceeds final normalization descriptively in {a["above"]}/{a["n"]} candidate/task/seed combinations. No new layer-to-layer interval or optimal-layer claim is introduced. All26 representations remain in the full atlas.'],'figure':'ANCHOR_READOUT_GAPS'}, {'title':'Adverse and inconclusive findings matter','paragraphs':[f'Original-base comparisons answer a different question. For candidate01, block16, seed42 and DEV AUROC, H3 refit minus base is {effect("example_emp_H3_independent_refit")}; splice refit minus base is {effect("example_gue_splice_reconstructed_independent_refit")}. Original base is not a proven immediate parent.',f'Ranking and probability quality can disagree: {dis["n"]}/{dis["eligible_prediction_cells"]:,} cells have higher AUROC but worse classifier cross-entropy than base. This is descriptive, not joint significance or a capability percentage. LM has54 primary DEV and54 diagnostic TRAIN units, not108 independent held-out evaluations.'],'figure':'ORIGINAL_BASE_EFFECTS'}, {'title':'Forget evidence, limitations and the next useful inputs','paragraphs':['Forget-related source logs recovered; qualified integration pending. The23 step-axis validation-loss observations and corresponding ppl values remain distinct from92 loss/ppl/both-axis display records. Reinit5 A has two step1500 values:1.3953843116760254 and1.3952388763427734. Both remain unresolved and preserved. Noise5 steps2000/2151 are separate endpoints, not independent seeds.','The configurations declare702 versus1 evaluation iterations. This is not a verified denominator. Exact checkpoint/invocation, metric/cohort/split, aggregation and implementation semantics remain unqualified. Layer-indexed gradient norms are diagnostics, not layerwise forget performance. No model-level loss is copied across layers.','Still needed: content-hash-bound validation/save receipts; producing evaluation source and cohort/aggregation metadata; compatible reference/uncertainty aggregates when available; genuine qualified layerwise forget-task aggregates. These belong in a separately versioned S10 assessment. Reuse all unaffected retain work; do not rerun the pipeline by default.','Conditional95% pointwise intervals describe fixed heads and cohorts, not intervention replication or familywise confidence. Unknown parent/mask/dose/exposure, partial delivery inventory and historical candidate05 privacy remain explicit limits. Current private protection cannot establish past visibility.','Evidence route: RESULTS.pdf and RESULTS.md; FIGURE_GALLERY.md for the complete111-figure retain atlas and source-log appendix; TABLE_INDEX.json and CLAIM_LEDGER.jsonl for exact rows; FRESH_CPU_RESTORE_CHECK.json for actual saved-analysis recovery residuals and locations; FINAL_RECEIPT.json for immutable delivery identities. No raw forget evaluation or collaborator messages were performed.']}]
